%% most one line of why. The reasoning lives in the module docstrings, which
%% can hold a paragraph without costing a page. Page width is fixed by the
%% renderer, so height is words: a label that grows shrinks the type.
%% EVERY LABEL LINE IS WRITTEN TO FIT, about 42 characters at wrappingWidth
%% 700. Leave a line longer and mermaid breaks it wherever it lands, which
%% is how "plus *two* / masks" and "103,044 · 960 / numbers" happened.

